# Line endings are part of the published artifact, so they cannot be a local
# preference. `clawhub skill publish` fingerprints file bytes; a CRLF working
# tree and an LF working tree of the same commit produce different fingerprints,
# and the registry then reports every skill as "content differs from published
# 1.0.0" (issue #26 — stale=9 on the Linux runner, stale=0 on the Windows
# machine the nine were published from).
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalizes to LF in the index and checks LF back out on
# every platform, including a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true. Local and
# CI then fingerprint the same bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary. Without this, `text=auto` still has to guess, and a false positive
# would corrupt the file on checkout.
*.gif binary
*.png binary

# Executed by CI and by `install.sh`; a CR at the end of a shebang line is a
# runtime failure, not a diff.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
